Use Han-only Ruby for the added Japanese terms, preserve Section IDs and old aliases, and record these as title clarifications. In particular `definitionとrelations` also has no Ruby: the Japanese particle does not distinguish its projected heading from the original.

All remaining seven headings, including the Article title, contain Ruby. The all-notes spelling adds reading text and consequently does not repeat the unchanged original heading. No other direct same-heading collision found. The saved actual historical GitHub anchor set is exact-source bound; this is a collision-risk assessment, not an actual generated GitHub uniqueness/navigation test. Verify every old/semantic destination after generation.

No clearly incorrect Ruby reading was identified in the heading check or the manuscript passages inspected. `既存/きそん` is an accepted reading and is not a defect to replace merely by preference. This limited follow-up is not a new exhaustive phonetic audit of every body annotation. No tracked files were changed and no generation was run.
